{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"94efa1105da5d7ef","name":"card_unit_1st_infantry_regiment_us","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_1st_infantry_regiment_us","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"1st INFANTRY REGIMENT","text":"After you deploy or add an infantry unit, it operates for free this turn.","flavorText":"The 1st Infantry Regiment, one of the oldest regiments in the US Army, served with the 6th Infantry Division during WWII. After training across the United States and later in Hawaii, the regiment deployed to New Guinea in February 1944. It took part in the New Guinea Campaign, including the assault at Sansapor, and received a Presidential Unit Citation for its actions at Maffin Bay. In January 1945, the 1st Infantry Regiment landed at Lingayen Gulf on Luzon as the 6th Infantry Division joined the campaign to liberate the Philippines. The regiment continued fighting across Luzon through the summer, remaining with the division for most of the campaign. Following Japan’s surrender, they moved to Korea in October 1945, where the 6th Infantry Division was tasked with occupation duties. The 1st Infantry Regiment remained there until its inactivation in 1949.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":3,"attack":3,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_1st_infantry_regiment_us","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_1st_infantry_regiment_us_title","SourceString":"1st INFANTRY REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"1st INFANTRY REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_1st_infantry_regiment_us_text","SourceString":"After you deploy or add an infantry unit, it operates for free this turn.","LocalizedString":"After you deploy or add an infantry unit, it operates for free this turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_1st_infantry_regiment_us_history","SourceString":"The 1st Infantry Regiment, one of the oldest regiments in the US Army, served with the 6th Infantry Division during WWII. After training across the United States and later in Hawaii, the regiment deployed to New Guinea in February 1944. It took part in the New Guinea Campaign, including the assault at Sansapor, and received a Presidential Unit Citation for its actions at Maffin Bay. In January 1945, the 1st Infantry Regiment landed at Lingayen Gulf on Luzon as the 6th Infantry Division joined the campaign to liberate the Philippines. The regiment continued fighting across Luzon through the summer, remaining with the division for most of the campaign. Following Japan’s surrender, they moved to Korea in October 1945, where the 6th Infantry Division was tasked with occupation duties. The 1st Infantry Regiment remained there until its inactivation in 1949.","LocalizedString":"The 1st Infantry Regiment, one of the oldest regiments in the US Army, served with the 6th Infantry Division during WWII. After training across the United States and later in Hawaii, the regiment deployed to New Guinea in February 1944. It took part in the New Guinea Campaign, including the assault at Sansapor, and received a Presidential Unit Citation for its actions at Maffin Bay. In January 1945, the 1st Infantry Regiment landed at Lingayen Gulf on Luzon as the 6th Infantry Division joined the campaign to liberate the Philippines. The regiment continued fighting across Luzon through the summer, remaining with the division for most of the campaign. Following Japan’s surrender, they moved to Korea in October 1945, where the 6th Infantry Division was tasked with occupation duties. The 1st Infantry Regiment remained there until its inactivation in 1949."},"operationCost":3,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPl